A private subnet requires an explicit outbound method for public endpoints. For an existing non-private subnet, Azure default outbound access may exist, but it is not a stable or dedicated egress IP and must be verified. Do not present either as the deployed state without checking the subnet and routes.

For connectivity investigations, distinguish client-to-service, session-host-to-service, session-host-to-profile-storage, DNS, authentication and transport issues. Verify effective NSGs, routes, proxy and private endpoint resolution where relevant.

