## 8. Maintenance and change management

- **Operational maintenance window:** `$MaintenanceWindow` (Local TimeZone of the Session Host : `$Location`). 
- **AVD agent update window:** `$MaintenanceWindow` (Local TimeZone of the Session Host : `$Location`). Do not infer it from the operational maintenance window. If configured separately, document its day, start hour, time zone and whether session-host local time is used.
- **Windows patching:** `<verify Update Manager or other patch schedule and maintenance configuration>`.
- **Image rollout:** `<verify deployment pipeline and change window>`.
- **FSLogix update:** `<verify approved image/policy process>`.

Before any host maintenance: confirm sufficient spare capacity, put the host in drain mode if approved, check active and disconnected sessions, notify impacted users as required, preserve rollback, and validate host registration and user sign-in afterward. Drain mode prevents new sessions but does not end existing sessions.

